---
source: tests/scaffold_layer_class.rs
expression: text
---
--- create meta-new:conf/layer.conf
# We have a conf and classes directory, add to BBPATH
BBPATH .= ":${LAYERDIR}"

# We have recipes-* directories, add to BBFILES
BBFILES += "${LAYERDIR}/recipes-*/*/*.bb \
            ${LAYERDIR}/recipes-*/*/*.bbappend"

BBFILE_COLLECTIONS += "meta-new"
BBFILE_PATTERN_meta-new = "^${LAYERDIR}/"
BBFILE_PRIORITY_meta-new = "6"

LAYERDEPENDS_meta-new = "core"
LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_meta-new = "wrynose"
--- create meta-new:README.md
# meta-new

Compatible with the Yocto Project series: wrynose.

## Dependencies

- `core`

## Adding the layer to a build

Run `bitbake-layers add-layer <path to meta-new>`, or add its path to `BBLAYERS` in
`conf/bblayers.conf`.
--- modify build:conf/bblayers.conf
# POKY_BBLAYERS_CONF_VERSION is increased each time build/conf/bblayers.conf
# changes incompatibly
POKY_BBLAYERS_CONF_VERSION = "2"

BBPATH = "${TOPDIR}"
BBFILES ?= ""

LAYERS_ROOT = "${TOPDIR}/.."

BBLAYERS ?= " \
  ${LAYERS_ROOT}/meta-core \
  ${TOPDIR}/../meta-vendor \
  ${TOPDIR}/../meta-mine \
  ${TOPDIR}/../meta-new \
  "
note: the layer is created in <ws>: a new layer must go in a directory that already holds a workspace layer (or the one `path` names), outside every existing layer
note: BBLAYERS in build:conf/bblayers.conf gets the new layer (a separate change in this plan)
note: to scaffold into meta-new later, list it in writable_layers in sous-chef.toml; sous-chef sees the layer once the workspace is discovered again (restart the server)
note: the new layer's files are not linted after the write: the layer is not part of the loaded workspace yet
